 {
  "formula_id": "formula_1",
  "section_path_id": "1~9",
  "section_ordinal": 21,
  "label": null,
  "representation": {
   "plain_text": "x -yz -y + zx &lt; 0 Factor terms: x(1 + z) -y(1 + z) &lt; 0 Factor out (1 + z): (x -y)(1 + z) &lt; 0 So, this inequality implies that (x -y)(1 + z) &lt; 0. Now, the second inequality: y -zx &lt; z -xy"
  },
  "source_digest": "1ef5ade198918a01bcbf13e7f5374c8d7caa1e27d2eaafaa173353675f13c9cc",
