  "section_ordinal": 21,
  "label": null,
  "representation": {
   "plain_text": "y -zx -z + xy &lt; 0 Factor terms: y(1 + x) -z(1 + x) &lt; 0 Factor out (1 + x): (y -z)(1 + x) &lt; 0 So, the second inequality is (y -z)(1 + x) &lt; 0. Now, combining both inequalities, we have: 1. (x -y)(1 + z) &lt; 0 2. (y -z)(1 + x) &lt; 0"
  },
